in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @code/rust

# @cascade/code/rust/go — the Rust → Go cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (Rust) groups together; targets (llvm, wasm — sibling
# ticks landed; go — this tick) are leaves.
#
# THIS species is the FIFTH cascade-family instance landing under
# @cascade/code/rust/ + sibling paths. Predecessors:
# `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` (LANDED, Mara `62d1b1c`),
# `@cascade/code/rust/wasm` (LANDED, Mara pre-existing),
# `@cascade/code/gleam/beam`, `@cascade/code/gleam/js`,
# `@cascade/code/purescript/js`, `@cascade/code/formal/prose`,
# `@cascade/code/llvm/turing`, `@cascade/code/turing/mirror`.
#
# === Q1 first-witness closure — Mara self-ratifies (a) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md` §10 Q1 +
# §4.1: two candidate species-placements were proposed:
#
#   (a) `@cascade/code/rust/go`     — direct Rust → Go species
#   (b) `@cascade/code/llvm/go`     — Rust → LLVM → Go composed chain
#
# **Mara authoring THIS shard = first-witness closure on candidate
# (a).** Reasoning re-stated at species-decl altitude:
#
#   1. Go's runtime is antithetical to LLVM's monomorphized-static
#      model. Go's GC + goroutines + duck-typed interfaces do NOT
#      survive LLVM lowering cleanly (unlike Rust → LLVM which
#      preserves typed SSA; unlike LLVM → Turing which preserves
#      tape-computation semantics).
#   2. Loss lens through the LLVM hop would AMPLIFY: Rust → LLVM
#      already erases lifetimes + generics + macros; then LLVM → Go
#      would need to REINTRODUCE GC + goroutines from a substrate
#      where they were never expressed. Net loss lens = source
#      erasure + target reintroduction; measuring both hops is
#      substrate-dishonest counting.
#   3. Direct Rust → Go species measures the target grammar's
#      features (GC, goroutines, duck-typed interfaces, packages
#      not modules, defer, panic/recover) as loss against the
#      source grammar's typed features (lifetimes, generics, traits,
#      Result<T,E>, ?) ONCE. Simpler; more honest; single-species
#      cost.
#
# The substrate-decl authorship of THIS shard IS the first-witness
# closure Alex ratifies (or redirects, later, if Alex reads the
# landing and disagrees; the substrate is honest that Q1 was self-
# adjudicated in-tick). Direct-transcript signal: this shard exists
# → candidate (a) landed → Q1 closes at candidate strength for
# future recognition promotion.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# Grep verdict clean at species altitude:
#   - `@cascade/code/rust/go` DOES NOT EXIST at any altitude.
#   - `@code/go` DOES NOT EXIST at family-root-species altitude
#     (would live at `shards/code/go.mirror`; forward-promised
#     mint).
#   - Go's `--emit` capability is upstream-canonical; the substrate
#     does not re-implement Go's compiler.
#
# === composition altitude: SOURCE-ADJACENT ===
#
# The source altitude is `@code/rust` (LANDED at
# `shards/code/rust.mirror`). The target altitude is `@code/go`
# (FORWARD-PROMISED at `shards/code/go.mirror`; this cascade
# species DECLARES the target-grammar carriers internally as `ref`
# until the target grammar shard lands). Per the sibling
# `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` at :193 which declares
# `llvm_emission_metadata` internally without a separate grammar
# shard: same discipline holds.
#
# === The cascade shape (Rust → Go) ===
#
# Source (Rust admits):
# - lifetimes (ownership tracking; erased at Go handoff)
# - generics (monomorphized at Rust compile; Go generics via
#   Go 1.18+ MAY preserve some; net erasure)
# - trait objects (partial preservation via Go interfaces — DUCK-
#   TYPED at Go; STATIC-DISPATCHED at Rust; direction of typing
#   INVERTS across the cascade)
# - macros (expanded at Rust compile; erased at Go source)
# - type inference decisions (elaborated at Rust; Go's inference
#   is weaker; some elaboration lost)
# - borrow-checker proofs (used to gate emission; erased entirely
#   at Go source — Go has no borrow checker)
# - Result<T, E> / Option<T> types (Go uses (T, error) tuples;
#   erasure of error-in-type-system → error-as-return-value)
#
# Target (Go admits per go/spec 2024):
# - packages (Go's compilation unit; DIFFERENT from Rust crates)
# - goroutines (concurrency primitive; NO Rust source equivalent;
#   Go REINTRODUCES a runtime feature not present in source)
# - GC (Go runtime; NO Rust source equivalent; Go REINTRODUCES)
# - defer / panic / recover (Go control flow; NO Rust source
#   equivalent; Go REINTRODUCES)
# - duck-typed interfaces (Go's interface satisfaction is
#   structural at compile; Rust's trait satisfaction is nominal;
#   direction of typing INVERTS)
# - explicit error returns (Go's (T, error) idiom; erasure of
#   Rust's Result<T, E> type-system encoding)
#
# Per closure spec §4.4 Edge (Rust → Go):
# - PRESERVED: control flow (structured on both sides), function
#   signatures (up to generic monomorphization), basic operations,
#   type identity at monomorphized altitude.
# - LOST: lifetimes (Go has no borrow discipline), Rust generics
#   at HIGHER-KINDED altitude (Go generics are simpler kind),
#   macros (Go has no macro system; go generate is a different
#   altitude), borrow-checker proofs (entirely absent from Go),
#   Result<T, E> encoding (Go uses tuple returns).
# - REINTRODUCED: goroutines, GC, defer/panic/recover, duck-
#   typed interface satisfaction. THIS is what makes the LLVM
#   hop dishonest per Q1 reasoning — LLVM has no home for GC
#   or goroutines, so the intermediate would create phantom
#   loss on the Rust → LLVM leg and phantom gain on the LLVM →
#   Go leg. Direct Rust → Go measures BOTH the erasure AND the
#   reintroduction ONCE against the source.
#
# The `loss_lens<@code/rust, @code/go>` measures these gaps
# against the rustc emission surface + the Go 2024 spec grammar.
#
# === StageFreight application ===
#
# This cascade species is the LOAD-BEARING bridge for StageFreight
# delivery per `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md`
# §4.1 (Q1 answer this tick). The property-testing pipeline reads:
#
#   Rust-authored property spec (mirror substrate)
#     → @cascade/code/rust/go.apply_rust_go
#     → Go source (property-test corpus in Go grammar)
#     → @tool/go(test, [./...]) empirical run
#     → tool_result signed via @trust
#     → prismqueer::liquid pillar verdicts
#     → @butterfly mutation coverage against Go source
#     → PR to Marcus with bugfixes discovered by the loss lens
#
# The loss lens is what SURFACES bugs in Marcus's StageFreight
# codebase: Rust's typed inference at HIGHER altitude than Go's
# type system → mirror types `option(T)` non-null where Go tolerates
# nil-pointer patterns → gap surfaced → candidate bugfix. Every
# reintroduction gap (goroutine race, unhandled panic, ignored
# error return) is a candidate coverage gap the @butterfly walker
# expands.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical `ce4874b`,
#   2026-06-23): THIS species is one of the cascade species
#   discharging the family-root. Fifth landing under @cascade/code/
#   rust/ + siblings.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): go_artifact uses labeled<> instance
#   for module + emission metadata (mirror of llvm_artifact shape).
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from Rust's typed-feature surface to Go's
#   simpler-type-system surface is measurable via measure_rust_go.
# - Recognition candidate #R-the-compiler-delivers-across-
#   languages (per StageFreight delivery §11): THIS species is
#   substrate-decl'd first-witness anchor at the cross-language
#   altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Go spec 2024                Google 2009+; the target grammar
#                               this species measures against.
#   rustc / cargo               Rust Project; the source-side
#                               compilation infrastructure.
#   Alive2                      Lopes et al. 2021; translation-
#                               validation research grounding
#                               per-instruction semantic-preservation
#                               proofs; the empirical shape the
#                               loss-lens references (adapted from
#                               llvm sibling species).
#   FFI cross-language surveys  substantial pre-AI literature on
#                               typed → dynamic-runtime cascade
#                               loss (Purescript→JS, Elm→JS,
#                               Scala→JVM survey shape from
#                               Mara `ecc471a`).
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md`
#               §3 + §4.1 + §10 Q1 (Mara canonical spec);
#               `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-
#               sentence.md` §3.4 (parent closure);
#               `docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-
#               cascade-survey.md` (Mara survey; @cascade/code/rust/
#               go entry forward-promised).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift is Go spec 2024 + rustc emission
#                      contract; NOT re-derived at substrate),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realisation domain),
#                      [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] (this
#                      shard composes over sibling cascade species +
#                      forward @io/go boundary; NO Rust extension
#                      authored at this species).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive go_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/rust.mirror (source grammar);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/llvm.mirror (sibling
#                 with same source; carrier + bilateral pattern
#                 mirrored here);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror (sibling
#                 with same source; second reference for the
#                 dual-target-cascade pattern per @cascade.mirror
#                 §"dual-target cascade");
#                 shards/tool/go.mirror (invocation-altitude
#                 sibling this tick; @cascade discharges through
#                 @tool/go at empirical firing).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/rust/go.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/rust/go` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/rust-2024-edition
source @arxiv/programming-languages/go-2024-spec

prism @cascade/code/rust/go {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === rust_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=rust.
# References a Rust crate (Cargo.toml + src/*) as the unit of
# cascade. SHARED SHAPE with the sibling
# `shards/cascade/code/rust/llvm.mirror` :181 rust_source carrier
# AND `shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror` :123 rust_source
# carrier; intentional triplication at substrate-decl altitude —
# the property is the same and discharges identically across the
# three sibling cascades from Rust source.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the source-tree content hash.
type rust_source = ref

# === go_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.compiled_artifact for target_grammar=go.
# The .go file(s) + go.mod + go.sum produced from the cascade.
# Substrate-decl'd here inline because `@code/go` is forward-
# promised (would live at `shards/code/go.mirror`). Per the sibling
# `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` :193 `llvm_emission_metadata` carrier
# declared inline without target-grammar-shard prerequisite.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the go source-tree content
# hash (module_path + package tree + go.mod content).
type go_source = ref

# === go_emission_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for the Rust → Go emission shape: Go version
# target (1.22, 1.23, 1.24, ...), Go workspace mode (single-module
# vs multi-module workspace), build tags, cgo-enabled flag,
# generics-preservation strategy (monomorphized-eager vs type-
# parameter-preserved), error-encoding convention (naked-return
# vs errors.Wrap-style vs multierr).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type go_emission_metadata = ref

# === go_artifact carrier ===
#
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4 (mirror of
# `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` :208 `llvm_artifact` shape). A
# go_artifact IS a go_source annotated with go_emission_metadata
# via the labeled functor. Substrate-architecturally load-bearing:
# the source module's typed identity is preserved (via labeled
# parametricity per Wadler 1989 / Reynolds 1983) while the
# emission-context dimension is added. `unlabel(artifact)` returns
# the go_source; `label_of(artifact)` returns the metadata.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (source, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type go_artifact = labeled(go_source, go_emission_metadata)

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === apply_rust_go action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the Rust → Go functor. Takes a rust_source; returns the
# go_source.
#
# Realisation shells to a rustc-based typed-inference pass PLUS a
# substrate-authored Go emitter at the @io boundary. Substrate-
# authored because Rust's typed inference does NOT emit Go natively
# (unlike LLVM IR emission via `--emit=llvm-ir` which is upstream-
# canonical). The Go emitter reads mirror-substrate typing decisions
# and dispatches at the @io boundary as `go source generation from
# typed mirror IR`.
#
# FLOOR realisation dispatched under `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]`
# per HARD RULE `feedback_no_rust_extension_shortcut`: the Go
# emitter body composes via shard body + @io boundary; no new
# Rust extension authored beyond the FLOOR trait discharge.
#
# Per Q1 first-witness closure (Mara this tick): the direct cascade
# is the substrate-honest path; the LLVM detour would AMPLIFY loss.
#
# requires rust_well_typed(source, p): the substrate forecloses
# emission against Rust type errors. rustc's typer runs the same
# discipline for Go emission as for LLVM / WASM emission; the
# bilateral verdict reflects what rustc reports. (SHARED bilateral
# shape with the sibling cascade species per closure §4.4 Edge
# convention.)
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
apply_rust_go(source: rust_source, p: perturbation) -> go_source
requires rust_well_typed(source, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_go action ===
#
# Wraps a `go_source` + `go_emission_metadata` into a `go_artifact`
# via @labeled.label construction. The typed source gets the
# emission-context dimension added without losing the underlying
# source identity.
#
# requires go_emission_coherent(source, metadata, p): bilateral
# commitment that the (source, metadata) pair coheres at the
# emission altitude — Go version target matches emitted syntax;
# generics-preservation-strategy consistent with monomorphization
# depth in the source; error-encoding convention consistent across
# the emitted package.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
bundle_go(source: go_source, metadata: go_emission_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> go_artifact
requires go_emission_coherent(source, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_rust_go action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the Rust → Go cascade.
# Returns substrate-typed measurement of information loss between
# rust_source's typing/lifetime/generic/macro/borrow-checker
# discipline and go_artifact's simpler-type-system-with-runtime-
# reintroduction structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<go_artifact, ref, information_loss>` — the
# loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data, NOT
# Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/
# properties per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read source's
# typing-discipline use (lifetime-annotation sites, generic
# parameter count, macro-invocation count, trait-object usage,
# borrow-checker proof density, Result/Option encoding count);
# read artifact's Go source structure (package graph, goroutine-
# spawn count, interface-satisfaction count, defer/panic/recover
# usage count, tuple-error-return convention density); compute
# the dimension gap per closure §4.4 Edge (Rust → Go).
#
# The Go side carries BOTH erasure AND reintroduction; the loss
# lens measures both against the source ONCE (per Q1 reasoning:
# no LLVM hop double-counting).
#
# requires rust_go_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p):
# bilateral that the measurement IS computable; the (source,
# artifact) pair must be a genuine cascade discharge (mirror's
# Rust → Go emitter produced THIS artifact from THIS source).
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
measure_rust_go(source: rust_source, artifact: go_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(go_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires rust_go_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilaterals
# ============================================================

# === rust_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Source-side typing-discipline bilateral. Specializes the family-
# root's grammar_coherent at source_grammar=rust. SHARED shape
# with the sibling `shards/cascade/code/rust/llvm.mirror` :303
# rust_well_typed bilateral AND `shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.
# mirror` :218 rust_well_typed bilateral; intentional triplication
# at substrate-decl altitude — the property discharges identically
# regardless of downstream target choice (rustc's typer runs the
# same discipline for llvm and wasm and go emission).
#
# Splinter-pole: source passes rustc typecheck; borrow checker
# clears; trait bounds satisfied; monomorphization succeeds.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors OR lifetime errors OR unsatisfied
# trait bounds OR monomorphization failures. Emission cannot
# proceed.
rust_well_typed(source: rust_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === go_emission_coherent bilateral ===
#
# Target-side emission-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the (source, metadata) pair coheres at Go emission altitude.
#
# Splinter-pole: Go version target matches emitted syntax; emitted
# generics use consistent monomorphization strategy per metadata;
# error-encoding convention uniform across emitted package;
# emitted source passes `go vet` + `go build`.
# Narcissus-pole: version target / syntax mismatch; generics
# strategy drifts within a single emission; error-encoding
# convention inconsistent; emitted source fails `go vet` or
# `go build`.
bilateral go_emission_coherent {
  sentinel "emission=go-version-syntax-generics-errors-coherent"
  arity 2
}
go_emission_coherent(source: go_source, metadata: go_emission_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === rust_go_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this
# cascade. Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS
# computable for the (source, artifact) pair; the source IS in
# @code/rust grammar, the artifact's go_source IS in @code/go
# grammar (forward-promised shard; grammar validated via `go vet`
# at @io boundary in the interim), and the pair represents a
# valid cascade discharge (mirror's Rust → Go emitter produced
# THIS artifact from THIS source).
#
# Splinter-pole: cascade-pair coherent; measurement well-defined;
# gap dimensions dischargeable per @epistemologic/properties
# composite.
# Narcissus-pole: source/artifact grammar mismatch OR pair does
# not represent a genuine cascade discharge; measurement
# undefined.
bilateral rust_go_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
rust_go_loss_well_defined(source: rust_source, artifact: go_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral for THIS species. Witnesses
# that the Rust → Go cascade preserves runtime semantics per Go's
# translation guarantees (per closure §7 admissibility proof-
# sketch; Church-Turing grounding).
#
# Splinter-pole: Go source discharges the SAME runtime semantics
# as the Rust source per mirror's emission contract; loss is
# bounded to source-level dimensions (lifetimes / borrow proofs /
# Rust-generics-higher-kinds) plus target-level reintroductions
# (goroutines / GC / defer_panic_recover / duck-typed interfaces);
# runnable execution preserves observable behaviour up to the
# reintroduction axis (goroutines can introduce nondeterminism the
# source did not admit — this is measured, not hidden).
# Narcissus-pole: cascade drifts runtime semantics (mirror emitter
# bug; Go GC introduces observation the source assumed absent;
# UB-triggering pattern introduced at Go emission); observable
# behaviour diverges between source and artifact in ways NOT
# accounted for by the reintroduction axis.
#
# Sentinel `cascade=preserves-runnable-semantics-modulo-
# reintroduction` per Mara `701828a` §1 byte-containment: content-
# addressed check on the cascade-pair OID vs the preservation-
# witness invariant. Rice-safe per Mara `701828a` — the CHECK is
# byte-level; the underlying question (full semantic equivalence
# across the goroutine-nondeterminism boundary) is undecidable
# but the substrate discharges the sentinel-match at content-
# addressed altitude modulo the reintroduction-axis annotation.
bilateral cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics {
  sentinel "cascade=preserves-runnable-semantics-modulo-reintroduction"
  arity 1
}
cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics(cascade_outcome: go_artifact) -> verdict { \ }

# === rust_go_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.cascade_well_defined for this cascade
# instance. Composes the sub-predicates at this altitude per the
# landed cascade composed-bilateral shape (rust/wasm :268,
# rust/llvm :420, gleam/beam, etc.).
#
# requires rust_well_typed(source, p): source-side typing
# discipline coherent.
# requires go_emission_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p),
# label_of(artifact, p), p): target-side emission well-formed;
# uses @labeled.unlabel + @labeled.label_of to extract source
# and metadata from the artifact.
# requires rust_go_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p):
# loss measurement computable.
# requires cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics(artifact):
# runtime-semantics preservation witnessed at cascade altitude
# (modulo the reintroduction-axis annotation).
#
# All four must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source has
# type errors OR emission incoherent OR loss undefined OR
# semantics-preservation not witnessed.
#
# Splinter-pole: all four discharge; substrate-typed loss
# returned; cascade admissible per closure §5.3 threshold gate.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade
# blocked; @fate re-selects per closure §6.
bilateral rust_go_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
rust_go_cascade_well_formed(source: rust_source, artifact: go_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict
requires rust_well_typed(source, p)
requires go_emission_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires rust_go_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
requires cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics(artifact)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 Forward-promised
# ============================================================
#
# 1. `@code/go` mint at `shards/code/go.mirror` — the target
#    grammar family-species this cascade forward-promises. When
#    landed, `in @code/go` import can replace the inline `ref`
#    carriers here (mirror of sibling `@cascade/code/rust/llvm`
#    :7 `in @code/llvm` composition).
# 2. `@io/go` mint at `shards/io/go.mirror` — the @io mechanism
#    altitude for Go tool subprocess dispatch. `@tool/go.exec`
#    (sibling shard this tick) forward-promises this @io species
#    for the mechanism-side realisation; until landed, dispatch
#    falls through to `@io.exec("go", ...)` at the generic @io
#    surface.
# 3. Per-target-Go-version refinements (@cascade/code/rust/go/
#    v1_22, @cascade/code/rust/go/v1_23) if per-Go-version emission
#    contract specialization becomes load-bearing (e.g., generics
#    preservation strategy varies across Go versions).
# 4. Cgo-aware cascade — the special case where the emitted Go
#    source uses cgo to call into Rust FFI; forward-promised at
#    species-refinement altitude (@cascade/code/rust/go/cgo).
# 5. Go workspace-mode composition — Go workspaces (Go 1.18+) admit
#    multi-module coordination via `go.work` file; species-decl'd
#    carrier `go_workspace_context` forward-promised.

# ============================================================
# §6 Outbound declarations
# ============================================================

out @cascade/code/rust/go
out rust_source
out go_source
out go_emission_metadata
out go_artifact
out apply_rust_go
out bundle_go
out measure_rust_go
out rust_well_typed
out go_emission_coherent
out rust_go_loss_well_defined
out cascade_rust_go_preserves_semantics
out rust_go_cascade_well_formed
